        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "test(shared): add unit tests for listener notify and register helpers",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe `notifyListeners` and `registerListener` utilities in `src/shared/listeners.ts` have no dedicated unit tests, leaving the event listener management primitives unverified against regressions.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdds comprehensive unit test coverage for both exports:\n\n**`notifyListeners`:**\n- Calls every registered listener with the event\n- Handles empty iterables without error\n- Continues to other listeners when one throws (error isolation)\n- Calls onError callback with the thrown error\n- Does not call onError when no listener throws\n- Works with Set as an iterable\n\n**`registerListener`:**\n- Adds the listener to the set\n- Returns an unsubscribe function that removes the listener\n- Unsubscribe is idempotent (calling twice is safe)\n\n## User Impact\n\n- Purely additive: one new test file, no production code changes\n- No risk of breaking existing behavior\n\n## Evidence\n\n```\n$ npx vitest run src/shared/listeners.test.ts\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  9 passed (9)\n```",
